AEngCwnZ1l0cfXNCrSpKk0.M; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Secure; Path=/; Domain=api.anthropic.com,]73:23:Content-Security-Policy,42:default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none',]23:12:X-Robots-Tag,4:none,]33:6:CF-RAY,20:9e7fdf96bf409090-DUB,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}7:request;3299:4:path;22:/v1/messages?beta=true,9:authority;0:,6:scheme;5:https,6:method;4:POST,4:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;18:1775468870.1369257^15:timestamp_start;18:1775468870.1359737^8:trailers;0:~7:content;2044:{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan: Distributed Tracing with Context Propagation for Track Cache\n\n## Context\n\nTrack is a GCD-based Swift 5 two-tier (memory + disk) LRU cache with no existing observability. The goal is to add distributed tracing: every public method creates a child span under the caller's context (if provided), records structured attributes, async evictions propagate their originating context, and the tracing backend is fully swappable via a protocol.\n\nConcurrency model: concurrent `DispatchQueue` + `DispatchSemaphore`. No Swift actors. Callback-based async.\n\n---\n\n## Files to Create / Modify\n\n| File | Action |\n|------|--------|\n| `Track/Tracing.swift` | **Create** ‚Äî all protocol abstractions and no-op implementations |\n| `Track/MemoryCache.swift` | **Modify** ‚Äî add traceContext to all public methods, eviction spans |\n| `Track/DiskCache.swift` | **Modify** ‚Äî add traceContext to all public methods |\n| `Track/Cache.swift` | **Modify** ‚Äî add traceContext, thread context through 3-level async chain |\n\n"}]}],"system":[{"type":"text","text":"x-anthropic-billing-header: cc_version=2.1.92.c67; cc_entrypoint=cli; cch=c5ac5;"},{"type":"text","text":"You are Claude Code, Anthropic's official CLI for Claude."},{"type":"text","text":"Generate a short kebab-case name (2-4 words) that captures the main topic of this conversation. Use lowercase words separated by hyphens. Examples: \"fix-login-bug\", \"add-auth-feature\", \"refactor-api-client\", \"debug-test-failures\". Return JSON with a \"name\" field."}],"tools":[],"metadata":{"user_id":"{\"device_id\":\"c50e88c830c8acad53e140253de1ecd562e8e2d53f8dd90059f4cf32f2a46495\",\"account_uuid\":\"\",\"session_id\":\"b695fd8b-199b-44d6-bd57-28b489dc6bd8\"}"},"max_tokens":32000,"temperature":1,"output_config":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"stream":true},7:headers;981:29:6:Accept,16:application/json,]31:13:Authorization,10:[REDACTED],]36:12:Content-Type,16:application/json,]51:10:User-Agent,33:claude-cli/2.1.92 (external, cli),]68:24:X-Claude-Code-Session-Id,36:b695fd8b-199b-44d6-bd57-28b489dc6bd8,]28:16:X-Stainless-Arch,5:arm64,]25:16:X-Stainless-Lang,2:js,]26:14:X-Stainless-OS,5:Linux,]40:27:X-Stainless-Package-Version,6:0.80.0,]31:23:X-Stainless-Retry-Count,1:0,]30:19:X-Stainless-Runtime,4:node,]41:27:X-Stainless-Runtime-Version,7:v24.3.0,]29:19:X-Stainless-Timeout,3:600,]173:14:anthropic-beta,150:interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14,redact-thinking-2026-02-12,context-management-2025-06-27,prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05,structured-outputs-2025-12-15,]52:41:anthropic-dangerous-direct-browser-access,4:true,]35:17:anthropic-version,10:2023-06-01,]26:9:x-api-key,10:[REDACTED],]14:5:x-app,3:cli,]28:10:Connection,10:keep-alive,]28:4:Host,17:api.anthropic.com,]46:15:Accept-Encoding,23:gzip, deflate, br, zstd,]25:14:Content-Length,4:2044,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}6:backup;0:~17:timestamp_created;18:1775468870.1361642^7:comment;0:;8:metadata;0:}6:marked;0:;9:is_replay;0:~11:intercepted;5:false!11:server_conn;4102:3:via;0:~19:timestamp_tcp_setup;18:1775468423.1141136^7:address;27:17:api.anthropic.com;3:443#]19:timestamp_tls_setup;18:1775468423.1624973^13:timestamp_end;0:~15:timestamp_start;18:1775468423.0885146^3:sni;17:api.anthropic.com;11:tls_version;7:TLSv1.3;11:cipher_list;0: